## Anti Pattern

- [ ] **Inconsistent naming**: Mixed conventions
- [ ] **No versioning**: Breaking changes without version bump
- [ ] **Overloading POST**: Using POST for everything
- [ ] **Missing error codes**: Vague error messages
- [ ] **No pagination**: Returning unbounded results
- [ ] **Sensitive data in URL**: PUT params in GET
- [ ] **Missing rate limiting**: No abuse protection
- [ ] **No authentication**: Unprotected endpoints

## Best Practice

- [ ] **RESTful conventions**: Follow REST principles
- [ ] **Semantic versioning**: Clear version strategy
- [ ] **Consistent naming**: Use nouns for resources
- [ ] **Comprehensive errors**: Detailed error responses
- [ ] **Pagination**: Always paginate lists
- [ ] **Security first**: Auth, validation, rate limiting
- [ ] **Documentation**: OpenAPI/Swagger specs
- [ ] **Idempotency**: Safe to retry

